        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): Talk camera flip control and microphone selection",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOn Android, `camera.snap`/`camera.clip` default to the front camera whenever the agent omits `facing`, with no user control — the user holding the phone cannot point the agent's eyes at the world. Microphone input has no user selection either: routing is automatic Bluetooth-priority only, with the audio source hardcoded.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe user preference becomes the default facing for capture commands; explicit agent `facing`/`deviceId` parameters still override, preserving agent-directed capture. Mic selection augments (never replaces) the existing automatic routing: an explicit choice is honored when the device is present and falls back to automatic when it is unavailable, rejected, removed, or rerouted.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- New flip control in the Talk session screen (Material flip-camera icon, label naming the target), shown only when the device actually has both front and back cameras; the choice persists.\n- Voice settings gain a microphone picker: \"Automatic\" plus hot-plug-aware input devices; changing it during capture is marked as applying to the next session.\n- Devices persist by stable key (type + address + product name) — never the reboot-unstable numeric device ID.\n- Preferred routing uses `AudioRecord.setPreferredDevice`, confirms the actual route after startup, and permanently falls back to automatic Bluetooth-priority routing for that session when the choice cannot be honored.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Play-debug Kotlin compilation + 35 focused JVM tests (SecurePrefs, camera-facing resolution, audio input session): passing — independently re-verified via `:app:testPlayDebugUnitTest` (BUILD SUCCESSFUL).\n- Ktlint main/test: clean. Android i18n parity: 1,489 keys across 21 locales (strings PR-authored per repo convention). `git diff --check`: clean.\n- No protocol, Gradle, dependency, video-streaming, or camera-preview changes. Live device validation deferred: no physical device attached during authoring; behavior guarded by unit tests and existing capture paths.\n",
